  "previous_goal_turn": "progress: committed and pushed native selection menus and combined RGB UI qualification",
  "scope": "Native scientific Invert now uses admitted C++ full-image XOR or no-selection Replace, retaining the legacy-compatible route. It requires idle active owner and exact document-ID fields. Existing native packed area masks preserve holes/disconnected regions and explicit empty results. Every current native area kind is covered. Preparation/record staging precedes publication; changed inversions append the existing complete selection-creation record when recording, and malformed/owner/resource refusals leave source/history/recorder untouched. Pixels, dirty state, navigation and pixel Undo/Redo are preserved. Source samples are not read by API/SDK inversion. Selection command source descriptors and strict codec now admit preserve_ieee_float32; both nonfinite policies require scalar Float32, with no source-policy downgrade. All five composition modes, record validation/replay/rebind and exact source IEEE words are covered. Actual C++ HeadlessInputSession menu clicks qualify six source modes and record control identities/points; rendering itself may read the visible source. This is shared ImGui input, not OS/real ImageJ AWT/OpenGL acceptance or a new pinned upstream runtime fixture. Installed Python Editor exercises the same compiled owner separately. Installed SDK consumers link only the public core, proving literal complements, three source policies, below-estimate refusal and no provider/sample reads; nonfinite datasets retain their established eager admission, while finite uses a throwing virtual provider. Initial compilation caught a deleted default request initializer; corrected to aggregate construction. Initial Python fixtures incorrectly assigned a copied crosshair and supplied a floating corner diameter; corrected fixtures only. The resource refusal worked, but an initial test regex expected budget instead of the existing working-memory-limit message; corrected assertion wording only. Initial SDK nonfinite virtual fixtures were refused by existing eager admission; corrected to admitted eager sources, preserving the finite throwing provider. GCC then rejected binding an rvalue transaction to the public lvalue commit parameter; named the transaction and reran both installed SDK consumers. All preceding7066 installed test IDs remain in each final7255 run;92 new inversion/policy cases and97 additional existing rounded-creation regressions explain the increase. Final native and Python checks have zero failures/errors/skips. Source manifests bind551 compiled inputs; tested installs/carriers, actual menu observations, SDK executables, reports and logs remain. Disposable environments, SDK builds, test fixtures and standalone raw roots were archived and CRC/every-member-SHA verified before confined removal. No requirement family, historical verification run, Auto expectation or original99 triple is reclassified.",
